    "html": "<p>When a square-shaped coil of side length <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"r\"></span> is rotated in a magnetic field, the induced emf in the coil is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\varepsilon\"></span>. Then the square-shaped coil is replaced by a circular coil with diameter <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"4r\"></span> that has four times as many turns. The speed of rotation is decreased sixteen-fold.</p>\n<p>What is the best estimate for the induced emf in the circular coil?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3 \\varepsilon\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"B\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"12 \\varepsilon\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"C\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"24 \\varepsilon\"></span></li>\n<li data-label=\"D\"><span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"48 \\varepsilon\"></span></li>\n</ol>"
